YOUR TASK: Complete this task: Implement the Lagrangian 8-state parity DP solution in Python: for each test case, double all X/Y/Z values, precompute them scaled by M=N+1, run an unrolled 8-mask max-plus DP maximizing encoded (score,count) with transitions new[m]=max(old[m], old[m^1]+(2X-beta)*M+1, old[m^2]+(2Y-beta)*M+1, old[m^4]+(2Z-beta)*M+1), binary search the largest beta in [0, 2*max_coord+1) whose final state 0 selected count is at least 2K, then output score//2 + beta*K; validate on the provided samples and small random brute-force cases.